---
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import Screenshot from "./Screenshot.astro";
import Card from "./Card.astro";
import agents from "../assets/agents.png";
import { REPO } from "../config";

// The plugin, one way in per tool. The note beside a command is the tool it
// is typed into, which is the only thing that distinguishes them: all of them
// install the same server and the same note for the agent.
const slug = REPO.replace("https://github.com/", "");
const installs = [
  { cmd: `/plugin marketplace add ${slug}`, note: "Claude Code, then" },
  { cmd: "/plugin install gitwarren@gitwarren", note: "" },
  { cmd: `gemini extensions install ${REPO}`, note: "Gemini CLI" },
  { cmd: `npx skills add ${slug}`, note: "the note alone, into any agent" },
];

// One click for the server alone, in the tools that publish a link format for
// it. Every link carries the same command the MCP registry entry names, so a
// tool that reads the registry and a tool that reads this link agree.
const server = { command: "npx", args: ["-y", "gitwarren", "mcp", "--serve"] };
const config = JSON.stringify(server);
const addTo = [
  {
    name: "Cursor",
    href: `cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install?name=gitwarren&config=${Buffer.from(config).toString("base64")}`,
  },
  {
    name: "VS Code",
    href: `https://vscode.dev/redirect/mcp/install?name=gitwarren&config=${encodeURIComponent(config)}`,
  },
  {
    name: "Kiro",
    href: `https://kiro.dev/launch/mcp/add?name=gitwarren&config=${encodeURIComponent(config)}`,
  },
  {
    name: "Goose",
    href: `goose://extension?cmd=npx&arg=-y&arg=gitwarren&arg=mcp&arg=--serve&id=gitwarren&name=GitWarren&description=${encodeURIComponent("Code review on your own machine")}`,
  },
];

const chip =
  "inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-line-strong px-4 py-2 font-mono text-note text-ink transition-colors hover:border-faint hover:text-white";
---

<section
  id="agents"
  class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-page flex-col gap-stack px-gutter pt-section"
>
  <Eyebrow>Agents in the loop</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="max-w-[900px] font-display text-h2">
    Your agents take part in the review &mdash; they aren&#39;t just the subject
    of it.
  </h2>

  <p class="max-w-[730px] text-body text-muted">
    GitWarren ships an MCP server over stdio. Point Claude Code, Codex or any MCP
    client at it and it gets the same seventeen tools the app itself uses: open a
    review, read the whole discussion, reply in a thread, leave a comment on a
    line, resolve one. Ask an agent to explain its own diff, or to answer the
    question you left on line 40 &mdash; in the review, where the answer stays.
    Every machine you add runs its own, set up by one sentence you paste into
    whatever agent is running there.
  </p>

  <p class="max-w-[730px] text-body text-muted">
    Install it as a plugin and the agent also gets a note that teaches it when
    to open a review and how to answer your comments. Cursor, Codex, VS Code
    and Kiro read the same repository from their plugin screens.
  </p>

  <!-- `select-all` on each command so one click takes the whole line, and the
       note beside it never comes along. Same block as the one in TwoShells. -->
  <div
    class="mt-[6px] w-full max-w-[730px] overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-well p-card"
  >
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 font-mono text-note">
      {
        installs.map(({ cmd, note }) => (
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-4">
            <code class="text-accent select-all whitespace-nowrap">{cmd}</code>
            {note && <span class="text-faint whitespace-nowrap">{note}</span>}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="flex max-w-[730px] flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <span class="font-mono text-note text-faint">Or just the server:</span>
    {addTo.map(({ name, href }) => <a href={href} class={chip}>Add to {name}</a>)}
  </div>

  <Screenshot
    src={agents}
    alt="An agent review comment and a human reply in the same thread"
    caption="An agent’s comment and the reply, in one thread — attributed, and never mistakable for a person."
    class="mt-[28px] max-w-shot max-sm:hidden"
  />

  <div class="mt-[38px] grid grid-cols-1 gap-cards sm:grid-cols-2">
    <Card title="Always attributed">
      A machine-written comment is always marked as one, and the tool&#39;s name
      comes from the MCP handshake rather than from whatever the model decides to
      call itself that day.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Two agents stay two">
      Each MCP session is given its own id, so two agents working at the same
      time are told apart in the thread without either having to cooperate.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Yours to edit">
      You can edit or delete anything in a review. An agent is held to its own
      messages &mdash; it can fix its own typo, not quietly rewrite yours.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Never over the network">
      An agent talks to the GitWarren on its own machine, over stdio, reading
      real paths on a real disk. The part that crosses a network is the window
      you are looking at &mdash; never the agent.
    </Card>
  </div>
</section>
